  "answer": "The official OpenAI announcement post is:\n\n1. **OpenAI (@OpenAI)** — March 14, 2023, 17:00 UTC  \n   “Announcing GPT-4, a large multimodal model, with our best-ever results on capabilities and alignment: https://openai.com/product/gpt-4”  \n   https://x.com/OpenAI/status/1635687373060317185  \n   [web:5] [web:4] [web:14]\n\nRelated public posts from the same announcement window:\n\n2. **Greg Brockman (@gdb)** — March 14, 2023, 17:00 UTC  \n   “We’re releasing GPT-4 — a large multimodal model (image & text in, text out)…”  \n   https://x.com/gdb/status/1635687252616679426  \n   [web:9]\n\n3. **Peter Welinder (@npew)** — March 14, 2023, 17:01 UTC  \n   “GPT-4 is here: our smartest and most reliable model yet!”  \n   https://x.com/npew/status/1635687624047489024  \n   [web:13]\n\n4. **Sam Altman (@sama)** — March 14, 2023, 17:02 UTC  \n   “here is GPT-4, our most capable and aligned model yet… available today in our API (with a waitlist) and in ChatGPT+.”  \n   https://x.com/sama/status/1635687859494715393  \n   [web:12]\n\n5. **Mira Murati (@miramurati)** — March 14, 2023, 17:03 UTC  \n   “Unveiling GPT-4 — our large multimodal model that exhibits human-level performance on various professional and academic benchmarks.”  \n   https://x.com/miramurati/status/1635688069692293121  \n   [web:6]\n\n6. **The Verge (@verge)** — March 14, 2023, 17:06 UTC  \n   Coverage of the OpenAI announcement: “OpenAI announces GPT-4 — the next generation of its AI language model.”  \n   https://x.com/verge/status/1635688829792268307  \n   [web:7]\n\nThe company blog post linked from the official status is OpenAI’s GPT-4 release note (March 14, 2023): https://openai.com/index/gpt-4/ [web:1].",
